// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-10-07 (Wednesday): Today's date as pattern
// ============================================================================
// Weekly rotation slot: the calendar date itself drives the pattern. Today
// (IST) is 2026-10-07 -- day 7, month 10 (October), year 2026.
//
// THE DERIVATION (this is the whole point of the day):
//   Recent Wednesdays each found a different relationship between day and
//   month: a digit-sequence melody (08-26), three clock rates (09-02), a
//   true hocket when day==month (09-09), day/month used directly as two
//   independent grid-lengths for a dual-voice polymeter -- 16 vs 9 (09-16),
//   a single lead with per-token inline Euclidean flutters (09-23), and a
//   GCD fraction-reduction into a 10-against-3 polyrhythm when day/month
//   shared a factor (09-30). Today day (7) and month (10) share NO factor
//   (GCD(7,10)=1, same coprime relationship as 09-16's 16/9) -- but rather
//   than repeating 09-16's device (two separate grids running side by side),
//   this time the date's own two numbers become the two arguments of the
//   Euclidean rhythm algorithm ITSELF: `.euclid(7, 10)` -- Toussaint's
//   algorithm distributing day's 7 onsets as evenly as possible across
//   month's 10 steps. One voice, one mask, generated directly from the date,
//   rather than two grids or a handful of per-token ornaments.
//
//   The LEAD is written as a full 10-token phrase per bar (one token per
//   month-step) with real melodic shape -- the Euclidean mask then silences
//   3 of those 10 tokens each cycle, turning the date's own math into the
//   phrase's rests, rather than placing rests by hand.
//
//   Two structural tones anchor every phrase: tonic (scale degree 0) and
//   degree 3 (month's reach: 10 mod 7 = 3, overshooting one octave to land
//   on the scale's 4th). Day's own digit, played as the raw degree number 7,
//   also overshoots exactly one octave above tonic (7 mod 7 = 0) -- the two
//   date numbers, played as literal scale degrees, both fold back onto
//   structural tones, which is why they're used as the phrase's two peak
//   notes (CALL/TENSION below).
//
//   Four hand-written phrases cycle through: CALL (rises to the day/month
//   overshoot peak, ends open on degree 3), RESPONSE (answers downward,
//   dipping below tonic via negative degrees, resolves to tonic), TENSION
//   (same two overshoot peaks in reversed order, all leaps, ends open),
//   RESOLUTION (the exact retrograde of CALL, note-for-note reversed --
//   a real retrograde device, not just "a calmer phrase").
//
//   CYCLES = 27 = day-digit-sum (0+7=7) + month (10) + year-digit-sum
//   (2+0+2+6=10). setcpm(72) x 27 cycles / 60 = 22.5s.
//
// Scale: G minor -- fresh for this slot (last three Wednesdays used D major,
// A minor, E minor); the numbers are the idea, not the mode.
//
// NO DRUM KIT, deliberately, not by default: the Euclidean(7,10) mask IS
// this piece's audible pulse, generated straight from the date's own two
// numbers -- a metric kit underneath would just restate a pulse that's
// already there, the same reflexive-percussion failure MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md
// already flags.
//
// Arrangement, deliberately different from the last three Wednesdays: those
// each put a slow pan-breathing automation on the drone (year-digit-sum
// period). This week the drone stays completely still (pure tanpura
// convention, tonic+5th, no automation at all) -- the one piece of filter
// automation this week lives on the LEAD instead, its sweep period tied to
// DAY's own prime value (7), so the automation budget doesn't default to
// the same formula on the same layer every week.
//
// Instrumentation: synth basics throughout (supersaw / sine), per
// MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §2.5 -- no acoustic-instrument sample names.
//
// This is a DAILY quick clip, not a flagship set -- one continuous pattern,
// no alap/jor/jhala arc.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(72)
let CYCLES = 27 // day-digit-sum (7) + month (10) + year-digit-sum (10)

stack(
  // LEAD -- four alternating 10-token phrases (one token per month-step),
  // filtered through Euclid(7,10): the date's own two numbers (day=7
  // pulses, month=10 steps) decide which 7 of the 10 written notes actually
  // sound each cycle -- the date generates the rests, not a hand placement.
  // CALL rises to the day(7)/month(10) overshoot peak and ends open (3);
  // RESPONSE answers downward through tonic; TENSION revisits both peaks
  // in reversed order; RESOLUTION is CALL's exact retrograde.
  n("<[0 3 5 7 10 7 5 3 0 3] [3 0 -2 0 3 5 3 0 -4 0] [5 10 3 7 0 10 5 3 7 3] [3 0 3 5 7 10 7 5 3 0]>")
    .euclid(7, 10)
    .scale("G:minor")
    .sound("supersaw")
    .attack(.008).decay(.12).sustain(0).release(.05)
    .distort(.15) // acid taste layer, kept light so the Euclidean mask stays legible
    .lpf(sine.range(400, 2200).slow(7)) // sweep period = day's own prime value (7)
    .gain(.34)
    .pan(.65)
    .room(1.2),

  // BASS pedal -- the two structural tones (tonic 0, month's reach-degree
  // 3), switching every 7 cycles: day's own value, unaffected by month.
  n("<0 3>/7")
    .scale("G:minor")
    .sound("sine")
    .attack(1.1).release(1.6)
    .gain(.26)
    .pan(.3)
    .room(2.4),

  // DRONE -- tanpura convention, tonic/fifth, held for the full piece with
  // NO automation this week (deliberate contrast to recent Wednesdays'
  // pan-breathing drone -- see header note above).
  note("[g2,d3]/27")
    .sound("sine")
    .attack(1.5).release(2.2)
    .gain(.22)
    .pan(.5)
    .room(3.2)
)
